.policy "ruff-pgh003-blanket-type-ignore" revision 2
.description "Give type-ignore comments specific error codes instead of silencing every type error on the line; a blanket ignore hides new, unrelated problems."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PGH003 (pygrep-hooks): a `# type: ignore` or `# pyright: ignore` with no `[codes]`. Any `#` of the
// comment may start it; `type` and the colon must touch.
//   x = 1  # type: ignore                 ← PGH003
//   x = 1  # noqa # pyright:ignore        ← PGH003
//   x = 1  # type: ignore[attr-defined]   not reported
//   x = 1  # type :ignore                 not reported: not a type comment
#include "python/misc2-noqa.rr"

.violation PGH003(at: node) code "PGH003"
    "Name the error in brackets after `ignore`, as in `# type: ignore[attr-defined]` or `# pyright: ignore[reportAttributeAccessIssue]`, so other errors on this line still surface."
    suppress ruff "PGH003"
PGH003(c) :- type_ignore_blanket(c).
